+# Welcome Email Design
+
+## Goal
+
+Send a professional welcome email when a user creates an account through signup.
+The email should help the user take the next step immediately, ask for feedback, and point them to the ForkMesh docs and blog.
+
+## Trigger
+
+The email sends on account creation/signup.
+It does not send on later login, profile updates, verification resends, or password resets.
+
+## Recommended Behavior
+
+The existing signup verification email becomes a combined welcome and verification email.
+This keeps the first signup experience to one message instead of sending a separate welcome email and verification email at the same time.
+The existing confirmation link remains the primary call to action because email verification is still part of account activation.
+
+## Email Content
+
+The subject is `Welcome to ForkMesh`.
+The message greets the user by node name when available.
+The primary call to action is the email confirmation link.
+The body includes direct links to `https://forkmesh.com/docs` and `https://forkmesh.com/blogs`.
+The body asks for feedback about what was confusing, what felt missing, and what the user wants ForkMesh to support next.
+The message keeps a professional tone and avoids marketing-heavy copy.
+
+## Runtime Flow
+
+The Worker already routes signup and finalize flows through `_send_verification_email`.
+That helper will continue generating the deterministic verification token and confirmation URL.
+The helper will change the subject, plain text body, and HTML body to the new welcome email.
+The lower-level `_send_email` Mailtrap integration stays unchanged.
+If Mailtrap is not configured or the send fails, signup still succeeds and the existing admin verification queue fallback remains in place.
+
+## Testing
+
+Add a focused contract test for the welcome email helper.
+The test should assert that signup verification email content now includes the welcome subject, confirmation link, docs link, blog link, and feedback prompt.
+Run the targeted account endpoint tests after implementation.
+
+## Out Of Scope
+
+This change does not add a second email provider.
+This change does not add a new database flag for welcome emails because the email is replacing the current signup verification message.
+This change does not alter Cloudflare secrets or deployment configuration.
